// cli_mac.cla: the core suite's Mac/native front-end (test-suite-review
// Task 9's Mac-gate swap) -- swaps in for cli.cla in the Mac/native
// build; never both in one composition. Runs the full case list via
// `on App.launch` and reports, then quits -- same output cli.cla's own
// empty-args/`all` path produces. Its original Mac-gate boots
// (TestSuiteOnMac/TestSuiteOn68k) were both retired by test-consolidation;
// this file's remaining consumer is internal/cg68k/segment_test.go, which
// is why it was kept rather than deleted alongside those boots
// (test-consolidation 2026-08-06).
//
// Why `App.launch`, not `App.startCLI`/`App.startEmpty` (both tried and
// discarded during this task): cg68k.cla's non-UI program startup
// (cg68Program's entry-handler dispatch, its own comment: "entry-handler
// dispatch stub -- no event/arg marshaling yet (Task 11)") calls EVERY
// declared app-level handler unconditionally on a native boot --
// `App.launch`, `App.startEmpty`, `App.startCLI`, `App.openDocument`, all
// of them, whichever are present -- with no real platform-exclusivity
// logic (unlike the UI-program startup path a few lines above it in the
// same function, which correctly never calls `handler_App_startCLI` at
// all, matching Ch7's "startCLI never fires on the Macintosh"). Worse,
// `App.startCLI`'s own `args: list of string` parameter is never
// marshaled into a valid (even if empty) list on this path -- confirmed
// by direct probe: `args.count` read back as uninitialized garbage
// (1114067400 in one run), which corrupted a `for a in args` iteration
// downstream and hung the whole native boot with zero captured output
// (no crash, no exit -- just stuck). This is a real, pre-existing cg68k
// gap (a documented stub, not something this task's migration
// introduced) -- fixing it is a clarusc source change, out of this
// plan's scope (CLAUDE.md: "No clarusc source changes anywhere in this
// plan... STOP and escalate" -- flagged in the task report instead).
// `App.launch` sidesteps it entirely: it takes no parameters (nothing to
// marshal), and both the UI and non-UI cg68k startup paths call it
// exactly once, unconditionally, before anything else -- the same
// handler the now-retired testdata/suite/test_suite.cla used exclusively
// and the only one confirmed safe on this native harness.
on App.launch {
    var sel: list of CoreTest
    var results: list of TestResult

    sel.add(All)
    coreCliRunAndReport(sel, results)
}
